From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 09:46:10 +0200
Subject: [compiler] Skip loop back-edges when computing dominating_frame_state

The Turboshaft graph builder visits blocks in RPO order, so at
loop-header-visit time the back-edge predecessor's final_frame_state is
still default-Invalid. The existing predecessor-merge treated that
default as a value that disagreed with the forward-edge FS, fell back to
Invalid, and propagated Invalid through the loop -- stranding any
downstream Check* op whose dominating Checkpoint was emitted before the
loop. crbug/502439789 hits this in the inlined sort: a pre-loop
Checkpoint (#28) dominates a post-copy-loop CheckedTaggedToTaggedSigned,
but the side-effect-free copy loop wipes it out during the RPO merge.

The bailout is unnecessarily conservative. A FrameState is a valid
resume point for any program point which isn't also dominated by a
closer framestate. Skip back-edge predecessors in the header merge so
RPO visit order stops manufacturing a spurious disagreement.

Fixed: 502439789
Change-Id: I8c3f1d19f31b47b4aad21b62b5d96790a640711b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/7761805
Reviewed-by: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#106483}

diff --git a/src/compiler/turboshaft/graph-builder.cc b/src/compiler/turboshaft/graph-builder.cc
index 0825365557ae9048c01729d80f0e0480326a7197..1c85d35655fe88de9de6b2a7aadcfbcc8853ca3e 100644
--- a/src/compiler/turboshaft/graph-builder.cc
+++ b/src/compiler/turboshaft/graph-builder.cc
@@ -253,16 +253,23 @@ std::optional<BailoutReason> GraphBuilder::Run() {
                        predecessors[j]->rpo_number();
               });
 
+    // Skip loop back-edge predecessors: their final_frame_state hasn't been
+    // computed yet at header-visit time.
     OpIndex dominating_frame_state = OpIndex::Invalid();
-    if (!predecessors.empty()) {
-      dominating_frame_state =
-          block_mapping[predecessors[0]->rpo_number()].final_frame_state;
-      for (size_t i = 1; i < predecessors.size(); ++i) {
-        if (block_mapping[predecessors[i]->rpo_number()].final_frame_state !=
-            dominating_frame_state) {
-          dominating_frame_state = OpIndex::Invalid();
-          break;
-        }
+    bool first_fs = true;
+    for (BasicBlock* pred : predecessors) {
+      if (pred->rpo_number() >= block->rpo_number()) {
+        // Skipping loop backedge.
+        DCHECK(block->IsLoopHeader());
+        continue;
+      }
+      OpIndex pred_fs = block_mapping[pred->rpo_number()].final_frame_state;
+      if (first_fs) {
+        dominating_frame_state = pred_fs;
+        first_fs = false;
+      } else if (pred_fs != dominating_frame_state) {
+        dominating_frame_state = OpIndex::Invalid();
+        break;
       }
     }
 
